# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# OTRF external-validation workspace (external_validation/): generated,       #
# caches and temporary artefacts ONLY. Manifests, configuration, source       #
# documentation (README.md), and evaluation summaries/reports intended for    #
# version control are intentionally NOT listed here -- see external_validation/
# README.md "Safe folder cleanup" for the distinction between "safe to delete
# and regenerate" (handled by scripts/runs_otrf/12-cleanup-otrf-workspace.py)
# and "safe to gitignore" (this file): evaluation/, outputs_baseline/,
# outputs_rag/ and retrieval/ hold run evidence and dissertation-relevant
# summaries and are deliberately tracked, not ignored.
external_validation/prepared/neutral_inputs/
external_validation/logs/
external_validation/archive/
external_validation/tests/tmp/
external_validation/tests/_tmp/

# Raw third-party OTRF Security-Datasets clone (a ~600MB download, not
# authored content). Kept on disk at the repo root as the source pool that
# scenarios are selected/copied from into external_validation/source/; not
# meant for version control.
/Security-Datasets-master/

# Python caches for the OTRF external-validation code only. Scoped
# deliberately: this task's remit is the OTRF workspace, so caches elsewhere
# in the repository (e.g. scripts/runs/__pycache__, prototype/) are left
# untouched rather than swept by a broad top-level __pycache__/ rule.
scripts/runs_otrf/__pycache__/
external_validation/tests/__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
external_validation/.pytest_cache/
external_validation/tests/.pytest_cache/
